SCALING ANALYSIS
================
FFT (forward/inverse): exactly 4x per 2x N -- confirms O(N^2) bottleneck
  1024 -> 2048:  4.72 -> 18.91 ms  (4.00x)
  2048 -> 4096: 18.91 -> 76.43 ms  (4.04x)
  4096 -> 8192: 76.43 -> 307.89 ms (4.03x)

Poly mul: exactly 4x per 2x N
  512 -> 1024:   14.18 -> 56.84 ms  (4.01x)
  1024 -> 2048:  56.84 -> 226.34 ms (3.98x)
  2048 -> 4096: 226.34 -> 916.06 ms (4.05x)

Causation: basisCvt/ibasisCvt in gf64_additive_fft_hqc2026.c lines 297-313
is an explicit matrix-vector multiply -- O(N^2) per call. The FFT does one
basisCvt + one butterfly per direction, so per FFT: O(N^2) + O(N log N).
Poly mul does 2 fwd + 1 inv = 3 * (O(N^2) + O(N log N)) = O(N^2).
Fix: Chen 2018 Algorithm 1 recursive BasisCvt brings this to O(N log N).